---
source: crates/dreamd-cli/tests/cli_help.rs
expression: "nested2_subcommand_help(\"memory\", \"bisect\", \"start\")"
---
Start a bisect between a good and a bad ref, and check out the midpoint.

Endpoints are ref names or object ids a ref names. The good ref's timestamp must be strictly earlier than the bad ref's. Adjacent endpoints print the bad ref and start nothing.

Usage: start [OPTIONS] --good <GOOD> --bad <BAD>

Options:
      --good <GOOD>
          Last known good ref (name or 64-hex object id)

      --bad <BAD>
          First known bad ref (name or 64-hex object id)

      --auto-test <SCRIPT>
          Run SCRIPT with `sh -c` after each checkout and mark by its exit status (0 = good) until the first bad ref is found

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
